ield/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8d990b4-2260-5cad-b86e-1c9f1728ff2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8d990b4-2260-5cad-b86e-1c9f1728ff2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303688} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7d6dfa6-428d-5ed1-a2cc-0782413945e7" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3348921f-55bc-5086-9822-e663a15c74c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3348921f-55bc-5086-9822-e663a15c74c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302771} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeddb248-1cdc-59c9-a928-9e3f9cf2c4c7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72939cc6-3d0d-529a-9c8c-72658e0c2def" :question/math-academy-id "q-332584" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  | $\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  | $\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+(-5)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+1\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of a Particular Solution for Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab23c90-40c9-571e-9f79-118b3d83869d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302633} {:answer/id #uuid "3a80ddec-00b8-503c-9044-eea16655f16c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302821} {:answer/id #uuid "6db8df92-d1b5-5c11-b43b-cb019986b7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}(t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}])" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303128} {:answer/id #uuid "82d10db6-bb4c-56a3-bf37-7b4b1dc5a6f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303273} {:answer/id #uuid "b20fc247-c254-53ad-977d-2c3be69f1839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a80ddec-00b8-503c-9044-eea16655f16c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302821} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ba3146-873b-5a08-989f-9066e7c8cc72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24c639b5-3938-594c-bf24-83bf8b532823" :question/math-academy-id "q-332749" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]){e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined."}]}
